# Where this box's backups go — read by `just backup`, `backup-init`,
# `backup-list` (docs/admin-guide.md#backups).  Copy into site/ and fill in.
#
# This file is also handed to the restic container as its environment, so
# any credentials an s3:/azure:/sftp: repository needs go here too — and,
# because docker reads it as an env-file, NO QUOTES around values.

# Two repositories, never one: the data bundle (databases, the escrow's
# snapshot, uploads) and the secrets bundle (.env, fleet/*.env, site/).
# A stolen copy of either is useless without the other.  A path is a
# mounted share (campus: the secure file share); it must already be
# mounted — `backup` refuses a directory that isn't a repository.
BACKUP_DATA_REPO=/mnt/backup/almanac/data
BACKUP_SECRETS_REPO=/mnt/backup/almanac/secrets

# Two passwords, and they must differ.  Each comes from a FILE (0600, outside
# the repo) or a COMMAND (a password manager's CLI) — set one of the two per
# bundle.  Wherever the nightly run reads them from, keep a copy OFF this box:
# a password that only lives here dies with the box it was meant to outlive.
BACKUP_DATA_PASSWORD_FILE=
BACKUP_SECRETS_PASSWORD_FILE=
# BACKUP_DATA_PASSWORD_COMMAND=
# BACKUP_SECRETS_PASSWORD_COMMAND=

# Scratch space for the night's dumps (a fresh directory each run, removed
# after).  Needs room for one Mongo archive plus the Postgres dumps.
# BACKUP_STAGE_DIR=/var/tmp

# Azure Blob, if that's the target (repo: azure:<container>:/almanac/data):
# AZURE_ACCOUNT_NAME=
# AZURE_ACCOUNT_KEY=
